Something like:

```c
typedef void (*k_cpu_enabled_cb)(uint8_t cpu);

struct k_cpu_enabled_subs {
    sys_snode_t node;
    k_cpu_enabled_cb *cb;
};

void k_cpu_enabled_subscribe(struct k_cpu_enabled_subs *subs, k_cpu_enabled_cb *cb);
```

ie, Kernel will keep a list of subscribers to be called when a CPU is enabled. PM subsys can subscribe before Kernel starts. Does it sound reasonable?

